<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Super Downloads" description="Privacy Policy for Super Downloads.">
  <div class="legal">
    <a href="/" class="back">&larr; Back</a>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: October 25, 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Who We Are (Data Controller)</h2>
    <p>Super Downloads (“we”) is based in Spain (European Union). For anything related to this policy or your personal data, contact <a href="mailto:support@superdownloads.app">support@superdownloads.app</a>.</p>

    <h2>2. The App</h2>
    <p>The Super Downloads desktop application runs entirely on your computer. The App does not collect, store, or transmit:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>URLs you download</li>
      <li>Video content or metadata</li>
      <li>Browsing history or clipboard contents</li>
      <li>Personal information</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Anonymous usage stats.</strong> To count how many people use Super Downloads, and for nothing else, the App sends one anonymous message a day while it is in use. It contains only: a random install number created on your Mac (not derived from your Mac, your email or anything else about you), the App version, your Mac's processor type (Apple Silicon or Intel) and your macOS major version. The install number is replaced by a new one every 12 months. The message goes to PostHog Inc. (United States) with the IP address replaced by 0.0.0.0, location lookup turned off and no user profile created. We only count active installs with it: it is never linked to your email, to what you download or to this website's analytics. It is on by default. The welcome screen (or, if you installed an earlier version, a one-time notice) tells you before the first message is sent, and you can turn it off anytime in Settings › Share anonymous usage stats: nothing more is sent from that moment and the install number is deleted from your Mac. Legal basis: legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) in knowing how many installs are active. Because it is limited to audience measurement, it does not require prior consent under the audience-measurement exemption described by the CNIL and the AEPD; you can object at any time by turning it off.</p>
    <p>Settings and download history are stored locally on your device using standard application storage. This data never leaves your computer.</p>
    <p>The one exception is <strong>activation</strong> (see section 4): when you activate the App, it sends the email address you enter once, together with the App version, your Mac's architecture and macOS version, and the computer name used to tell your devices apart. Nothing about what you download is ever sent.</p>

    <h2>3. The Website — Anonymous, Cookieless Analytics</h2>
    <p>This website (superdownloads.app) uses PostHog to understand aggregate traffic — page views, referrers, browser and device type. This analytics setup is deliberately privacy-first:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cookieless:</strong> no cookies or local storage are used for analytics, so no consent banner is shown.</li>
      <li><strong>Anonymous:</strong> no user profiles are created and events are not linked to an identified person. To count unique visitors per day, PostHog computes an irreversible hash on its servers from your IP address, browser and a random value that changes every day and is then deleted; the hash cannot be traced back to you, and nothing is stored on your device.</li>
      <li><strong>No session recording:</strong> we do not record your screen, mouse movements, or keystrokes.</li>
      <li><strong>Aggregated only:</strong> we look at totals and trends, not individuals.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Analytics data is processed by PostHog Inc. on servers hosted in the United States. Transfers rely on PostHog's standard safeguards for international data transfers under GDPR.</p>
    <p><strong>Legal basis:</strong> legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) in understanding aggregate website usage, using anonymous, cookieless measurement that does not profile visitors.</p>

    <h2>4. Activation</h2>
    <p><strong>When you activate the App:</strong> Super Downloads is free, and activation asks for your email address. We store it, with the technical details listed in section 2, so we know who uses the App and can contact you about important changes to it (for example, security fixes or the end of the free period). After you activate, we may send you one welcome email with tips for using the App. <strong>Legal basis:</strong> performance of the free licence you request (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).</p>
    <p><strong>Updates and other Super apps (optional):</strong> the activation screen has a box, unticked, to receive emails about App updates and our other apps. We only send those emails if you tick it, and we store when you ticked it and the exact wording you agreed to. Versions 1.5.5 and earlier showed that box already ticked; we don't treat those as consent, so they get no such emails. You can withdraw at any time, from the one-click link in every email or by writing to us. <strong>Legal basis:</strong> your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR).</p>
    <p>Activation data is stored with our database provider, Airtable (Formagrid Inc., United States). Emails are sent through Resend (Resend Inc., United States). Both work under their standard safeguards for international data transfers.</p>
    <p><strong>When you contact support:</strong> we store your email and message content only to respond to your inquiry.</p>

    <h2>5. Other Third-Party Services</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>GitHub:</strong> the App and its updates are distributed via GitHub Releases, and the App downloads its yt-dlp component from GitHub. When you download from GitHub, GitHub's privacy policy applies to that connection.</li>
      <li><strong>yt-dlp:</strong> the open-source download component runs locally on your computer. Video downloads go directly from the source platform to your device — no video data or URLs pass through our servers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We retain activation email addresses for as long as you use the App or until you ask us to delete them, and support correspondence for as long as needed to resolve your inquiry. You can request deletion at any time.</p>

    <h2>7. Your Rights (GDPR)</h2>
    <p>If you are in the EU/EEA, you have the right to access, rectify, erase, and receive a copy of your personal data, to restrict or object to its processing, and to withdraw consent where processing is based on consent. To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:support@superdownloads.app">support@superdownloads.app</a> — we will respond within 30 days. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local supervisory authority (in Spain, the Agencia Española de Protección de Datos, <a href="https://www.aepd.es" rel="noopener">aepd.es</a>).</p>

    <h2>8. Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated date.</p>

    <h2>9. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy? Contact us at <a href="mailto:support@superdownloads.app">support@superdownloads.app</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>

